# Nkwa V Project Context

## Mission

Preserve, share, and certify African cultural heritage using Web3 (EVM blockchain + IPFS) with accessible Web2 UX.

## Architecture

```
frontend/          React 18 SPA (Create React App)
backend/           Node.js + Express 5 + Prisma + PostgreSQL
contracts/         Vyper smart contracts (cultural registry)
```

## Key Directories

- `backend/src/routes/` — API endpoints
- `backend/src/services/` — Business logic (Web3, IPFS, content)
- `backend/prisma/` — Database schema and migrations
- `frontend/src/pages/` — Route pages
- `frontend/src/components/` — UI components
- `frontend/src/contexts/` — React context providers

## Conventions

- JavaScript (not TypeScript) across frontend and backend
- Functional React components with hooks
- Express route handlers delegate to services
- Environment variables via `.env` (never committed)
- Tests in `__tests__/` directories

## Web3-Specific

- Gasless UX via backend relayer (`EVM_RELAYER_PRIVATE_KEY`)
- IPFS for decentralized content storage
- Contract interactions go through `backend/src/services/` — do not call chain directly from frontend
- See `WEB3_SETUP_GUIDE.md` and `DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` for setup

## Agent Skills

Skills from [addyosmani/agent-skills](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills) are in `.agents/skills/`. See `AGENTS.md` for lifecycle mapping. Apply relevant skills for each task — especially `security-and-hardening` for Web3 work.
